{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויבאו אילמה", :translit "va-yavo'u eilmah", :gloss "and they came to Elim"} {:he "ולא אמר ויחנו באילם", :translit "ve-lo amar va-yachanu be-eilim", :gloss "and it does not say 'they encamped at Elim'"} {:he "שלא היה דעתם לחנות שם", :translit "she-lo hayah da'atam lachonot sham", :gloss "that they did not intend to encamp there"} {:he "נס", :translit "nes", :gloss "miracle"} {:he "י\"ב עינות מים", :translit "y\"be einot mayim", :gloss "twelve springs of water"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Textual anomaly: verse says 'they came' but not 'they encamped' at Elim, until the springs were found; contrast with normal travel-stop formula."}], :frame {:text "Exodus 15:27 records that at Elim there were twelve springs of water and seventy palm trees, and Israel encamped there. The verse in Numbers 33:9 mentions the arrival at Elim but the phrase 'they encamped' appears after the springs are noted, suggesting the encampment depended on the discovery of the water.", :sources ["Exodus 15:27" "Numbers 33:9"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Textual anomaly: verse says 'they came' but not 'they encamped' at Elim, until the springs were found; contrast with normal travel-stop formula.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:32:39.557496139Z", :model "glm-5.2"}